# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READING OF THIS OUTPUT -- the three facts that matter on resume
#
# 1. IT IS NOT AN EQUILIBRATION PROBLEM.  With 5000 snapshots and 6x the walk
#    length of the legacy run, T/ne wanders 0.2-1.3 with no approach to the
#    legacy +1.746.  E/ne sits at -34.5..-35.7 against legacy -37.75, a ~2.1
#    gap that does not close.  So "walk longer" is NOT the fix, and no amount
#    of extra sweeps should be spent before the estimator is understood.
#
# 2. V IS CLOSE AND T IS NOT.  V/ne = -0.676 (this walk) / -0.6439 (the
#    regression-budget walk) against legacy -0.7448: a 9-14% difference.  T is
#    the wrong SIGN: clean ~+0.6, legacy +1.746, and the regression-budget walk
#    even read T/ne = -1.5281.  T carries the whole of the ~2.07 discrepancy.
#    A wrong sign in a kinetic energy is an estimator or wavefunction defect,
#    not sampling noise.
#
# 3. Im(T) IS LARGE.  mean 7.28, rms 26.29 per snapshot, against a T/ne of order
#    1.  For a wavefunction that is real up to a global phase -- which the
#    v = 0 liquid should be -- the local energy's imaginary part must average to
#    zero.  An rms this large is the single most suspicious number here and is
#    the first thing to chase.
